<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20868] build: make rpms ignores --with-systemdsystemunitdir=no</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20868</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;On RHEL &amp;gt;= 7, Fedora &amp;gt;= 18, SUSE &amp;gt;= 13.1 and openEuler, it is not possible to build RPMs without systemd support. Both ./configure --with-systemdsystemunitdir=no and rpmbuild --without systemd are silently overridden.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="code panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="codeContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre class="code-java"&gt;
# rpm -q systemd
systemd-257-13.el10.rocky.0.1.x86_64
# ./autogen.sh &amp;amp;&amp;amp; ./configure --with-systemdsystemunitdir=no --with-o2ib=/usr/src/ofa_kernel/x86_64/6.12.0-124.28.1.el10_1.x86_64/ &amp;amp;&amp;amp; make rpms
...
# rpm -qpl lustre-2.17.58_117_g7c3ac26-1.el10.x86_64.rpm | grep systemd
/usr/lib/systemd/system/lnet.service
/usr/lib/systemd/system/lsvcgss.service &lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
